# Upstream files this integration deliberately does not ship.
#
# pharmacy is a module inside TibaDesk, not a product with a website of its own.
# It brings a complete standalone marketing site — one advertising itself as a
# pharmacy management platform, with its own landing page, team page, product
# video and logo. routes/web.php used to answer / with that site, so the
# application presented a second website alongside TIBADesk-website, reachable
# on its own port and, to a signed-in user, at /apps/pharmacy/.
#
# It is removed rather than merely unrouted: any sync restores it from upstream,
# so a bare deletion in apps/ would not survive, and the route that served it is
# only one edit away from serving it again.
#
# Paths are relative to the application root, and are checked by
# bin/sync-apps.sh --verify — which is what catches a wrong prefix here.
# One path per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# Note that public/dashboard/ is NOT listed. That is the panel's own built SPA,
# not a website: it is the interface a pharmacy uses once signed in. It is also
# absent from this repository's source tree as editable React, so it is shipped
# pre-built and must not be removed.
public/website